strengths.value:
- The Clave framework presents an interesting split of responsibilities over a strong LLM that can extract arbitrary concepts from text, and a weaker LLM that is cheap to fine-tune and adaptable for changing value systems with few data samples;
- The ValEval dataset provides a robust basis for fine-tuning and evaluating LLMs on different ethical value systems;
- Three evaluation datasets are provided: i.i.d., perturbed, and o.o.d.;
- The benchmark results show strong adaptability and generalizability for Clave pairs;

opportunities_for_improvement.value:
- One of the main points of pairing weaker LLMs with stronger LLMs is the cost of fine-tuning; It seems crucial to know exactly how much performance is lost compared with just fine-tuning a stronger LLM, and/or having a more concrete price comparison of this approach vs using stronger LLMs;

_Typos_
- Line 241: Llama-2-7b-chat is a 7B parameter model (not 13B);

